Survival analysis models the time until an event occurs, which may not always be observed (i.e., it can be censored). In cancer survival prediction, a censored event indicates either patient survival or the last known follow-up time, while an uncensored event signifies patient death. We now detail the Negative log-likelihood and Cox proportional Hazards survival losses.
