Multi-panel scientific data visualization with panels labeled A, B, C, and D.

Panel A: Bar chart titled “Evaluation of Generic QA Samples on Slim Go Terms (Generated Answers vs. Ground Truth).” It compares fractions of GO term matching categories across three GO aspects: Biological Process, Molecular Function, and Cellular Component. Categories shown are “Overlapping GO Terms,” “Exact Matching GO Terms,” and “No Matching GO Terms.” The main finding visible is that overlapping GO terms dominate for all three aspects, exact matches are very low, and no-match fractions are highest for Biological Process.

Panel B: Bar chart comparing “Ground Truth Testset” versus “Generated” counts per GO term for the Cellular Component aspect. X-axis contains GO cellular component terms; y-axis is count. Paired blue and magenta bars show term-wise differences between ground truth and generated outputs.

Panel C: Wide bar chart comparing ground truth and generated counts per GO term for Biological Process. Numerous GO biological process terms are shown on the x-axis with rotated labels. The chart shows substantial term-specific variation, with some generated counts much higher than ground truth for certain processes.

