--- CHUNK 59 ---
G HCA Split: Hash Function Details
import hashlib
```
def cell_split(shard_idx: int, cell_idx: int) -> str: key = shard_idx * 50001 + cell_idx + 126 h = int(hashlib.md5(str(key).encode()).hexdigest(), 16) % 10 if h <= 7: return "train" elif h == 8: return "val" else: return "test"
```
This produces the approximate 80/10/10 split and is portable across platforms. The constants 50001 and 126 were chosen to avoid hash collisions between adjacent cells from different shards.
